{{/* @dot donseba/go-webthings-docs/internal/website.DocsArticleData */}}
<article class="grid max-w-5xl gap-6">
    {{ template "hero.gohtml" . }}

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Default behavior</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">With an error stage such as <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">ext/errors</code> registered, direct top-level failures render a useful error page. Region failures render an error section inside the parent output. Without an error stage, <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">partial.Write</code> writes nothing for a failed render and returns the error.</p>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">The optional <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">ext/errors</code> stage focuses on the template failure itself. In detailed mode it shows the partial ID, template list, request URL, extracted template location, and original render error. Import it as <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">exterrors</code>, so it does not clash with the standard library's <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">errors</code>.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Where boundaries apply</h2>
    <table class="w-full overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-800/90 text-left">
        <thead class="bg-slate-900"><tr><th class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 text-left font-bold text-slate-50">Failure</th><th class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 text-left font-bold text-slate-50">Result</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle">Top-level content fails during <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">partial.Write</code></td><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle">A full error page with status 500 for normal requests, or a swappable error fragment with status 200 for HTMX requests, because HTMX does not swap 500 responses by default. Both are sent with <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">Cache-Control: no-store</code>.</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle">Registered region fails inside a parent template</td><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle">The parent keeps rendering and the region position receives an error fragment.</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle">Selected partial fails inside <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">{{ "{{ selection }}" }}</code></td><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle">The selected tab or panel receives an error fragment while the rest of the page survives.</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">RenderWithRequest</code> returns an error</td><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle">The caller decides how to handle it. The embedded page is a writer-level behavior.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Development and production</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">The default extension mode is <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">exterrors.ModeSafe</code>. It shows the status text and a safe message (<code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">exterrors.SafeMessage</code>), and names no partial, template or error. During development, opt into <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">exterrors.ModeDetailed</code> to show the partial ID, template list, URL, template location, and original error.</p>

    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">root := partial.New("shell.gohtml").
    Use(exterrors.Stage(exterrors.WithMode(exterrors.ModeDetailed)))</code></pre>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Custom stage</h2>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">root := partial.New("shell.gohtml").
    Use(partial.RenderStageHooks{
        RenderFunc: func(ctx *partial.RenderContext, next partial.RenderNext) (template.HTML, error) {
            if ctx.Kind != exterrors.RenderKindError {
                return next(ctx)
            }
            return template.HTML("&lt;section&gt;Something went wrong&lt;/section&gt;"), nil
        },
    })</code></pre>

    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">The separate showcase app includes a live broken-template example. It keeps the shell in place and only replaces the failing content section.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Failing the whole response</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">By default (<code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">partial.FailInline</code>) a failing part of a page renders as its error fragment in place. With <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">FailResponse</code>, any failing or missing part fails the render: <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">Render</code>, <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">RenderWithRequest</code> and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">RenderSelf</code> return the first failure and no HTML, and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">Write</code> writes only the failure response of the error stage, or nothing without one, and returns the error.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">root.SetFailurePolicy(partial.FailResponse)

err := partial.Write(r.Context(), w, r, page)
var written *partial.FailureResponseError
if err != nil &amp;&amp; !errors.As(err, &amp;written) {
    // Nothing was written; answer with an error page.
    http.Error(w, "Something went wrong", http.StatusInternalServerError)
}</code></pre>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">When <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">Write</code> wrote the failure response of an error stage, it returns a <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">*partial.FailureResponseError</code> that wraps the render error, with the status it wrote; compare errors with <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">errors.Is</code>. With <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">FailResponse</code> the failure response keeps an error status for partial requests too and comes without out-of-band regions; with <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">FailInline</code> a partial request gets the error fragment with status 200, so the client swaps it in place.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Error templates of your own</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">The failure response can be a template of the application, such as a theme's 500 page, and the error fragment a toast. The template is read from the file system of the partial that failed and renders as its child, with its functions, stages, includes and models; its dot is an <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">exterrors.Data</code>. A root with <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">SetChildIncludes("partials/*.gohtml")</code> gives it the partials of the pages. When the template fails itself, the built-in markup answers.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">root.Use(exterrors.Stage(
    exterrors.WithTemplate("500.gohtml"),
    exterrors.WithFragmentTemplate("partials/error-toast.gohtml"),
))</code></pre>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">In the safe mode <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">Data.Message</code> is <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">exterrors.SafeMessage</code> and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">Data.Location</code>, <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">Data.PartialID</code> and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">Data.Templates</code> are empty, so a template can print the message; <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">Data.Error</code> holds the error in both modes, so show it only when <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">.Detailed</code>. <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">WithMessage(fn)</code> sets the message, such as to a translation in the request's language, <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">WithTitle(fn)</code> the heading (the status text by default) and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">WithLang(fn)</code> the page's <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">lang</code>. A stage with only a page template answers partial requests with it too, and one with only a fragment template full pages.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Errors as flash messages</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">With <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">exterrors.WithFlash(fn)</code>, a partial request that fails is answered with an error flash message, out of band in the flash target, with the template of the tree's <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">exp/flash</code> stage, and the target stays as it is (<code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">HX-Reswap: none</code>). Its text is the one <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">fn</code> returns, or <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">Data.Message</code> for a nil <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">fn</code>. Under <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">FailResponse</code> the status stays 500: with htmx 4, let the page swap the out-of-band parts of 5xx responses with <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">connector.Attr.KeepOnServerError</code>.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">root.Use(
    flash.Stage(flash.WithTemplate("templates/flash.gohtml")),
    exterrors.Stage(exterrors.WithFlash(nil)),
)</code></pre>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Errors outside a render</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">An error that happens outside a render, such as a form post whose handler fails to save it, gets the same answer with <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">exterrors.Respond(w, r, root, status, err)</code>: the error page, fragment or flash message of the stage registered on the root's tree, written with the status and never cached. A full-page request gets the error page; a partial request gets the error flash message with <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">WithFlash</code>, else the error page for a 5xx status and the error fragment for another status. Without a stage it answers with the built-in markup in the safe mode. <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">partial.WriteError</code> is the core of it, for any error stage.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">if err := comments.Add(r.Context(), form); err != nil {
    log.Error("add comment", "error", err)
    exterrors.Respond(w, r, root, http.StatusInternalServerError, err)
    return
}</code></pre>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Content-Security-Policy</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">The built-in error page styles itself with one inline <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">&lt;style&gt;</code> element, so it looks right when the application's own assets are what failed: add <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">exterrors.StyleHash()</code> to <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">style-src</code> under a policy without <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">'unsafe-inline'</code>. The built-in fragment has classes only (<code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">go-partial-error</code>, <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">go-partial-error__title</code>, <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">go-partial-error__message</code>, <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">go-partial-error__details</code>): serve the stylesheet of <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">exterrors.StylesheetFS()</code>, <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">partial-errors.css</code>, or style the classes in the application's CSS.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">policy := "default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' " + exterrors.StyleHash()</code></pre>
</article>


